            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KRISB"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Personally, I adore mojakko (unless it's kalamojakka, ask an American Finn about that), but mojakko isn't eaten in Finland. It's kind of the Finnish-American equivalent of green beer."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nathan L Niemi"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this boiled dinner (Mojakka) with a ham base. I boil down a smoked hammock for stock, add all the vegies: onion, carrots, rutabaga, potatoes, and for the last 10 mins cabbage. Spices are pepper, allspice, garlic, accent, and bay leaves. Then add about two cups of chopped ham. Hmmmmm on a cold winter day... Of course a good homemade bread makes it even better!",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-25T14:34:14.693Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lilfoo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic way to use unsexy roots like rutabaga. Thanks to everyone who provided feedback, I modified the recipe to include the following: 2 stick butter - cut it down to 0.5 stick butter; ½ teaspoon ground black pepper - replaced with 10 pepper corns; 4 potatoes, cubed - replaced with rutabaga; added 3 bay leaves; added 3 allspice berries. The recipe also doesn’t tell it, but I assumed that the meat had to be cut into cubes before being fried in butter. I found that the recipes uses way too much butter. I should have tried before judging, but using quarter of the butter produced very good result in my opinion. The soup was very flavourful, meat was tender and veggies preserved their taste, the broth was the best part! I will be making the soup again!",
            "datePublished": "2024-01-13T15:29:07.643Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "juurainen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this soup/stew many times... I also add 3 whole allspice, 2 bay leafs, rutabaga , and parsnips, this is a root vegetable soup after all... This is a great recipe to build off, to suit your family needs/likes... Thanks for the share... :)",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-30T08:40:47.760Z"
          },
          {
